### Scientific baseline cross-check (`/api/analyze_region`, same epoch pair)

- Status `ok`, mean |significance| = **2.12**, **50 candidates** at ≥5σ on the WCS-aligned, noise-normalized map.
- **38 of 50 coincide with Gaia DR3 stars** (within 10″), so the majority are most plausibly known-star variability/drift, not new objects.
- Top: `significance-074` at RA 76.852277, Dec 30.340581, score 196.3, area 7 px — matches Gaia DR3 156336573353358976 at 2.14″ (G=9.41, 15 mas/yr PM).
- Other top matches: `significance-087` (149.6, Gaia sep 6.6″), `significance-032` (138.2, sep 7.0″), `significance-092` (134.1, sep 5.8″).

The OpenCV pass (110) is **not** a superset or upgrade of the baseline (50); it is a lower-selectivity display threshold on rendered RGB, so it over-counts relative to the noise-normalized significance map.

