**Caveats:** I could not visually inspect the montage — this model does not support image input — so all counts above come from the JSON reports. The explorer's auto threshold is not written into the JSON. No `fetch_region` was needed. Sign is relative to the rendered stretch, not calibrated photometry. SPHEREx's linear-variable filters can change apparent brightness between visits without true variability.

**Standing caveat:** Every OpenCV hit is an unclassified visual aid requiring scientific validation — never a confirmed detection. The `/api/analyze_region` noise-normalized result is the stronger baseline, and even its candidates remain unclassified.
